.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/settings.local.json

# Rust
/target/
**/target/
!src/target/
!src/target/**
# Isolated per-worktree cargo target dirs (CARGO_TARGET_DIR=target-<name>)
/target-*/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
# ...but the PDB type-recovery lane's fixture is COMMITTED: the lane must run
# on a clone with no Windows toolchain. Same reason as the canary .so files.
!tests/pdb_types/*.pdb
!tests/pe_identity/*.pdb

# Scratch output from local gate/benchmark runs (result maps, dumps, logs).
# Never a source of truth: the committed artifacts are baseline.json and
# structural_baseline.json.
/workspace/
# Don't ignore Cargo.lock for binary projects
